# acidcandy — SPEAK (syllable-per-note formant) demo + the muted-303 tripwire (2026-07-28).
#
# READ THIS FIRST IF A 303-DRIVEN A/B COMES BACK BYTE-IDENTICAL:
# both 303 lines are MUTED at boot by design (mac[] initialisers: "MUTED by default — bring it in on
# record"). So a plain `script /dev/null` render of this cart is DRUMS ONLY. Anything hanging off a
# 303 note-on — SPEAK's vow_attack() is exactly that — can never fire in a default render, and
# ab-render will correctly report ALL VARIANTS BYTE-IDENTICAL. That is not a broken feature, it is an
# untriggered one. This cost a real debugging round; the two clicks below are the fix.
#
# It also means any master-FX measurement taken WITHOUT these clicks describes the formant on an
# 808+909 kit, not on the acid line. Re-measure through this script when the 303s matter.
#
# The LED coordinates are measured, not guessed (crop the top 14 rows of a --dump frame and scale 8x:
# each cartridge's mute LED is the rightmost <=9px of its tab). 303a LED (37,8) · 303b LED (61,8).
#
# To hear SPEAK you need three things, and the cart boots with NONE of them:
#   1. a 303 sounding      -> the two clicks below
#   2. the VOWEL device armed  -> MST face -> FX -> tap VOWEL -> ON   (see 05-fx-hub-vowel.script)
#   3. SPK lit                 -> the SPK key next to ON
#
# Verified with 1 + vowon/vowspeak forced on (isolated save-dir so live saves are safe):
#   vstep walks the word 0..7 with ZERO skips and vcur takes ~200 distinct values -> it GLIDES through
#   each syllable rather than jumping (the glide is what makes it a diphthong, not a click).
#   The voice GATE (vgate) dips to 0.000 on the word's two REST slots: 23% of frames sit below 0.25,
#   matching 2-rests-in-8-slots. One pause frame by frame, showing the asymmetric envelope:
#     0.98 -> 0.44 -> 0.20 -> 0.09 -> 0.04 -> 0.02 -> 0.01 -> 0.19 -> 0.33 -> 0.45 -> 0.63
#     (snap shut, hold closed, ease back in — a stop consonant into a vowel)
#
# THE PAUSES ARE WHAT MAKE IT READ AS SPEECH, and the numbers say so. Spectral centroid over time:
#     static vowel (SPK off) : mean 2201 Hz  std 1281 Hz
#     word, NO pauses        : mean 2287 Hz  std 1270 Hz   <- std UNCHANGED: a gapless vowel stream
#                                                             moves the spectrum no more than a
#                                                             STATIC vowel does. It slurs, it does
#                                                             not speak.
#     word WITH pauses       : mean 2799 Hz  std 1964 Hz   <- +55% variance = audible phrase boundaries
#
# TWO BUGS THIS FILE EXISTS TO CATCH (both found by tracing, both invisible by ear alone):
#   1. DOUBLE-ADVANCE. Both 303 lines feed one word, so notes landing on the same tick advanced it
#      TWICE in a frame and SKIPPED slots — and a skipped REST is a pause that never happens (vstep
#      walked 0,2,4,6 and only 6% of frames paused). Fixed by vowfired: one syllable per frame.
#      If vstep ever skips again, that regressed.
#   2. TOO-SLOW CLOSE. A pause lasts one note (~6.8 frames for a 16th at 132 BPM) but easing shut on
#      the GLID slew needed ~7 frames to even reach 0.25, so the mouth never finished closing and the
#      pause was an inaudible dip. Fixed by making the gate asymmetric (snap closed 0.55, ease open on
#      GLID). If the paused-frame share falls back toward single digits, that regressed.
#
# PAUSING IS TWO ORTHOGONAL KNOBS, both present only while SPK is lit (5 knobs then: GLID DENS GAP Q MIX).
#
# GAP = how DEEP each pause goes. Swept, 500 frames each:
#     GAP 0.0 -> gate floor 1.000   0% paused   centroid std 1290 Hz   (= the gapless slur)
#     GAP 0.5 -> gate floor 0.500   0% paused   centroid std 1597 Hz   (a dip, not a stop)
#     GAP 1.0 -> gate floor 0.000  23% paused   centroid std 1964 Hz   (full stops, the default)
#
# DENS = how MANY pauses, via a per-slot VOW_RESTAT[] threshold rather than randomness, so rests arrive
# in a fixed hand-authored order and every setting is repeatable:
#     DENS 0.00 -> resting slots {}          0% paused   std 1275 Hz
#     DENS 0.25 -> {7}                      12%          std 1740 Hz   (one breath at the phrase end)
#     DENS 0.50 -> {3,7}                    23%          std 1964 Hz   (the default, two breath groups)
#     DENS 0.70 -> {3,5,7}                  36%          std 2267 Hz
#     DENS 0.95 -> {1,3,5,7}                48%          std 2457 Hz   (a rest every other note)
# Slots 0,2,4,6 carry threshold 9.0 and can NEVER rest — they are the strong syllables.
#
# THE EQUIVALENCE GATE worth re-running after any word/threshold edit: DENS 0.5 must reproduce the
# hard-coded two-breath-group word BYTE-IDENTICALLY (both were sha e1b1dc2c3c6e56a7 on this script at
# 500 frames). That is what proves a knob carved out of a constant added a control without moving the
# sound. If that sha drifts, the default voicing changed and someone needs to have meant it.
#
#   node tools/play.js acidcandy script tools/clips/acidcandy/06-speak-vowel-per-note.script \
#        --headless --frames 400 --trace /tmp/spk.jsonl
#   # then read the vspk/vstep/vcur/vtgt watches (frame lines are the ones WITHOUT a "vev" key)
#
# HEADS UP, this cart AUTOSAVES: play.js renders into the LIVE build/saves/acidcandy/, so running this
# script through it persists the unmute into the rolling autosave and changes where you resume next
# time. Harmless but surprising. To measure without touching the live save, drive the built binary
# directly with its own save dir (this is how the numbers above were taken):
#   cd build && mkdir -p saves/_tmp && ./acidcandy-dbg --script <this file> --headless --frames 400 \
#        --save-dir saves/_tmp --trace /tmp/spk.jsonl --wav /tmp/spk.wav
click 12 37 8      # 303a cartridge LED -> unmute the bass line (else nothing feeds vow_attack)
click 24 61 8      # 303b cartridge LED -> unmute the lead line
